Z||000000||Bob||10-04-2001||09:56 PM||||Hey I am new to the whole Fiero scene, but I am really interested in building up a Fiero of my own. I just have a few starter questions, What are some sites that have Fiero info/modifications? How much time/money (rough estimate) goes into an engine swap (3800 Series II)? What year Fiero would be best to purchase, anything I should look for when buying a Fiero? Any tips to help me get on my way are gladly accepted. <P>(sorry about posting in wrong forum, first time post en all...)<BR>------------------<BR>1997 Pontiac Grand Prix GTP -lotsa mods, so little room...<p>[This message has been edited by Bob (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||10-04-2001||10:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bob:<BR><B>Hey I am new to the whole Fiero scene, but I am really interested in building up a Fiero of my own. I just have a few starter questions, What are some sites that have Fiero info/modifications? How much time/money (rough estimate) goes into an engine swap (3800 Series II)? What year Fiero would be best to purchase, anything I should look for when buying a Fiero? Any tips to help me get on my way are gladly accepted. <P>(sorry about posting in wrong forum, first time post en all...)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Bob.. Welcome to the Fiero world. Theres tons of people here with extensive mods. Good Luck..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>-Haze<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">              .              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">        <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Jefrysuko||10-04-2001||10:18 PM||||Welcome,<BR>For websites first check out the link for "Fiero parts vendors" on the bottom of each page.  I don't have much knowledge about the 3800 swap but there is a guy here selling a 3800 series II with around 25k for $750 but he is here in Illinois.  There are a few places out there in CA that do the wiring for the swap (I am sure someone will give some info on that).  There really isn't a better car to have when it comes to Fiero's.  The 88s have a better suspension but there are more aftermarket parts for 84-87 and can be made to handle just as well if not better.  Watch for rust in the battery tray and upper corners of the trunk (just pull the carpet up and peek).  The best way for you to find info is to do a search on the forum.  You will be amazed on what you will find.<BR>If you want to tell us what you have done to your GTP I am sure we would all like to know.<BR>Jeffrey<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Zippy_11_sig.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jefrysuko||10-04-2001||10:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> Hey Bob.. Welcome to the Fiero world. Theres tons of people here with extensive mods. Good Luck..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>-Haze<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You beat me by 1 min.  I'll get you next time though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ray b||10-04-2001||10:27 PM||||hi Bob the 88 is the best year , better sept and brakes[vented disk] formula for the v6<BR>gt's are heavyer and cost more.<BR>to do a 3800 swap bigest headacke is to swap the computer and wires unless you want/musthave a 5 spd stick auto is way eazyer/cheaper<BR>cost is 2500 to 12,000 depends on what you do yourself and how good you wheel and deal. <BR>fieroman had a site with do it yourself info<BR>try a search on his name<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
