Z||000012||85ZainoGT||10-05-2001||12:49 PM||||well if you need a car, check my post in the mall section, my 85gt is for sale for $2200<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||terryk||10-05-2001||04:25 PM||||Bob, you're in California so unless you register the car in another state, you will have to stick with the automatic on the 3800 engine. California will not re-certify the engine on a manual trans.<P>Depending on the year of the engine you will need a 4T60E or 4T65E.<P>Series I SC 92-95 4T60EHD<BR>Series II SC 96 4T60EHD<BR>Series II SC 97-02 4T65E<P>I think the NA engines stayed with the 4T60E a year or two longer.<P>There is an advantage to the 96 combo. You can install that, get it blessed by BAR and then swap to the 94/95 ECM which works with that engine and trans (with a new chip). Otherwise you are at the mercy of the few people that will re-flash the 96 and up PCM if you want any performance tuning. <P>If you can find an 88, that's great. Nice suspension, but if you can't, there's nothing wrong with an 85-87.<P>TK<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||1
